{
  "contract": "saven.postgres-business-rules",
  "version": 1,
  "status": "design-and-schema-input",
  "date": "2026-11-15",
  "owner_contract": "PIVOT-003",
  "applies_to": [
    "db/postgres/20-tenant-schema.sql reference domain annotations",
    "tenant_data.reference_values seed rows per tenant",
    "tenant_data.business_rule / approval_policy / posting_constraint / tax_profile versioned JSON"
  ],
  "extension_rule": "A new value in any domain below is an active/effective-dated tenant_data.reference_values row, not a migration and not a code constant. A new executable behaviour requires a registered typed handler plus tests; storing a JSON row never installs logic. Used policy rows are superseded with a new version, never mutated. Application and posting-kernel validation is authoritative; this file is the canonical seed list and JSON-schema registry, and it is not itself a live policy engine.",
  "authority_notes": [
    "AI-origin ledger documents are ordinary documents with document_status PENDING_APPROVAL and origin_type ai. There is no ai_proposal table.",
    "ai_origin_direct_post_allowed defaults to false and must remain false in Phase 1.",
    "Monetary values in tenant ledgers are exact integer minor units (bigint). Approval thresholds are exact numeric decimals. No floats are used anywhere.",
    "A reference value can change the configured set of labels/domains; it can never grant protected owner authority or install posting logic.",
    "D-013/D-014: a posted entry can be terminally voided through the audited atomic primitive; the source stays retained and immutable, and voided entries are readable by normal module access. Fine-grained visibility is future application RBAC, never a database role rule."
  ],
